      "kind": "text",
      "text": "Program Format:"
    },
    {
      "kind": "text",
      "text": "Full-time, four-year program."
    },
    {
      "kind": "heading",
      "level": 1,
      "text": "Admission Information",
      "links": [
        {
          "text": "Admission Information",
          "url": "https://www.torontomu.ca/calendar/2026-2027/programs/fcad/creative_industries/"
        }
      ]
    },
    {
      "kind": "text",
      "text": "O.S.S.D. with six Grade 12 U/M courses including Grade 12 U English. Notes:"
    },
    {
      "kind": "list_item",
      "text": "ENG4U/EAE4U is the preferred English."
    },
    {
      "kind": "list_item",
      "text": "A grade of 70 percent or higher will be required in Grade 12 U English."
    },
    {
      "kind": "list_item",
      "text": "Subject to competition, candidates may be required to present averages/grades above the minimum."
    },
    {
      "kind": "heading",
      "level": 1,
      "text": "Program Overview/Curriculum Information",
      "links": [
        {
          "text": "Program Overview/Curriculum Information",
          "url": "https://www.torontomu.ca/calendar/2026-2027/programs/fcad/creative_industries/"
        }
      ]
    },
    {
      "kind": "text",
      "text": "Core courses develop your competencies in communication, digital technology, critical thinking, research design, collaboration and teamwork while informing you about the economic, legal, political and technological environment in which Canadian and international creative enterprises function."
    },
    {
      "kind": "text",
      "text": "As you proceed through the program you select two Creative-Content Modules from Table II to focus your studies. These modules of five courses offer students exposure to creative fields, including film, television, live performance, music, publishing, news media and fashion. You’ll learn about the historical, creative and production aspects of these fields while examining how they function as businesses, both domestically and globally. At the same time, you undertake several business courses that provide you with the foundational business, management and entrepreneurial skills vital to your future career. The interdisciplinary design of the program and the broad range of elective choice give you the flexibility to shape your studies to fit your personal interests and aspirations. You may also elect to combine your program with a minor in another discipline. The University’s downtown location in Canada’s media, artistic and financial capital provides an ideal setting for the study of the Creative Industries and for your work between your third and fourth year."
    },
    {
      "kind": "heading",
      "level": 2,
      "text": "Liberal Studies"
    },
    {
      "kind": "text",
      "text": "Students must take three lower level liberal studies courses and three upper level liberal studies courses to graduate. Students must not choose courses that are restricted for their program or major.",
      "links": [
        {
          "text": "lower level",
          "url": "https://www.torontomu.ca/calendar/2026-2027/liberal-studies/table_a/"
        },
        {
          "text": "upper level",
          "url": "https://www.torontomu.ca/calendar/2026-2027/liberal-studies/table_b/"
        }
      ]
    },
    {
      "kind": "text",
      "text": "Please refer to the liberal studies chapter of this calendar for more information on the Liberal Studies Policy. Further information on liberal studies can also be found at the Faculty of Arts' Liberal Studies website (opens in new window) .",
      "links": [
        {
          "text": "liberal studies",
          "url": "https://www.torontomu.ca/calendar/2026-2027/liberal-studies/"
        },
        {
          "text": "Liberal Studies website (opens in new window)",
          "url": "https://www.torontomu.ca/content/ryerson/liberal-studies/"
        }
      ]
    },
    {
      "kind": "heading",
      "level": 2,
      "text": "Minors"
    },
    {
      "kind": "text",
      "text": "Students may pursue any Minor offered by Toronto Met (with some exceptions). Please refer to the Minors chapter of this calendar for further information on individual Minor requirements and exclusions.",
